# Native host ABI

The physical Wasm32 boundary between compiled Moth and native Rust host code.

## Contract

- Input: canonical binding identities and signatures from the external-package registry, the restricted host-binding profile, builder-selected facade exports, the variant's `ValidatedMemoryPlan` and the build-owned target assignment
- Output: host imports and selected export wrappers using fixed scalar carriers, string spans, staged-text tickets, option tags, result frames, resource tokens and one immutable host manifest per artefact
- Decides: boundary carriers, frame layouts, status and tag values, import naming, reserved helper and export names and the staged-text and call-scope protocols
- Must not decide: Moth semantics, source legality, internal Moth storage representations, memory strategies, Rust signature mapping or runtime resource-table, staging-table or fault policy
- Invariant: ordinary Moth values cross as independent, non-retained values, the error channel stays distinct from success slots and no boundary layout repairs or infers a missing compiler fact

## Main paths

- `src/compiler_frontend/external_packages/`
- `src/backends/wasm/hir_to_lir/imports.rs`
- `src/backends/wasm/runtime/imports.rs`
- `src/build_system/build.rs` (package assembly and export selection)

